{"id":"NCT07020819","title":"An Open Label Clinical Study to Evaluate Tanruprubart (Also Commonly Known as ANX005) in Participants With Guillain-Barré Syndrome (FORWARD Study)","official":"An Open-Label Study to Evaluate the Pharmacokinetics, Pharmacodynamics, Efficacy, and Safety of a Single Dose of ANX005 in Participants With Guillain-Barré Syndrome","summary":"The goal of this open label study is to measure pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics, early efficacy, and safety of tanruprubart in adult and pediatric participants, in the United States, Canada, and Europe.","conditions":["Guillain-Barre Syndrome"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Tanruprubart"}],"criteria":"Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Diagnosis of GBS according to the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke Diagnostic Criteria for GBS.\n* Onset of GBS-related weakness ≤10 days before start of infusion on Day 1\n* GBS-disability score (DS) score of 3, 4, or 5 at screening and before start of infusion on Day 1.\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* Previous or planned treatment with either plasma exchange or IV immunoglobulin within 90 days of Day 1.\n* Diagnosis of any form of GBS that does not involve weakness of the extremities.\n\nOther protocol-defined criteria may apply.","minAge":"8 Years","maxAge":"85 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":30,"start":"2025-09-12","pcd":"2027-05-31","upd":"2026-10-26","sponsor":"Annexon, Inc.","areas":["neurology"],"central":["Study Coordinator · 1-650-822-5500 · clinicaltrials@annexonbio.com"],"sites":[{"f":"St. Joseph's Hospital & Medical Center - Barrow Neurological Institute (Dignity Health)","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85013","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"HonorHealth Bob Bové Neuroscience Institute","city":"Scottsdale","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85251","s":"R","lat":33.5092,"lon":-111.899,"c":""},{"f":"Profound Research LLC","city":"Carlsbad","pr":"California",